                <h2>Weekly Compliance Highlights</h2>
<p>As Q4 enters its critical phase, all three major advertising platforms have simultaneously tightened their compliance policies. Three significant changes have been observed this week:</p>
<p><strong>Meta</strong> expanded pre-approval requirements for cryptocurrency, forex, and digital asset ads to cover secondary page redirects; <strong>TikTok</strong> added specific definitions for "trademark-infringing content" in its community guidelines, covering video thumbnail text and audio trademarks; <strong>Google Ads</strong> now requires all ads targeting EU users to clearly identify the data processing entity.</p>
<p>This means ads that were running normally last week may now trigger review delays or account restrictions. YiyuMedia's compliance team completed inspections of 23 key accounts this week, identifying issues concentrated in three main areas.</p>
<h2>High-Risk Area 1: Account Credentials and Authorization Chain</h2>
<p>Approximately 40% of account suspensions this week were not due to creative violations but rather expired credentials or broken authorization chains. Common issues include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Business license scope doesn't match the advertised products</li>
<li>Authorization letters missing legal representative signature or official seal</li>
<li>Expired industry certification documents still in use</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Recommended Action</strong>: Log into each platform's ad dashboard to check expiration indicators in "Account Information - Verification." Establish a 30-day advance warning mechanism. YiyuMedia's backend now includes credential expiration alerts, pushed alongside balance warnings.</p>
<h2>High-Risk Area 2: Creative Copy and Visual Elements</h2>
<p>Review rejection rates increased 15% week-over-week this week. High-frequency triggers include:</p>
